Third-party software bundled into the Akuma devbox image
========================================================

neatvi (editor, shipped as /bin/vi)
-----------------------------------
  Upstream:  https://github.com/aligrudi/neatvi
  Author:    Ali Gholami Rudi
  Pinned:    e0fff2c05329caccfd22a99bde0f7e666a2334a4 (default when this was written;
             overlays/devbox/bootstrap.sh clones --depth 1 and prints the exact commit
             used for each build).
  License:   See the LICENSE / COPYING notice in the upstream repository. neatvi is
             distributed under permissive terms by its author; it is bundled here
             unmodified and cross-compiled with aarch64-linux-musl-gcc.

The devbox also stages the standard Akuma userspace (busybox, apk, tcc, scratch, meow,
etc.) whose provenance is tracked in the main repository and its submodules
(.gitmodules). NetBSD-derived rump kernel sources carry their own attribution in
userspace/rumpkernel and src-netbsd.
